<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Banu Ifran emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">742 CE – 1066 CE (approx.) · capital Tlemcen</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Zenata Berber emirate centred on Tlemcen, born from a Kharijite revolt and later a power in Morocco under Córdoba's overlordship.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-ifran">Banu Ifran</a> were a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanata-berbers">Zenata Berber</a> tribe of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. In the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> revolt against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> from 740, they embraced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufriyya">Sufri Kharijism</a>, and around 742 their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-qurra">Abu Qurra</a> established a state at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a>, where he was proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-qurra">Abu Qurra</a> raised large armies and joined the siege of the Abbasid governor at Tobna in 772. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a> fell to Idris I of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/idrisid-dynasty">Idrisid dynasty</a> around 790, but the tribe stayed powerful. In the 10th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yala-ibn-muhammad">Ya'la ibn Muhammad</a> founded the town of Ifkan and allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/caliphate-of-cordoba">Caliphate of Córdoba</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a>. Later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-ifran">Ifranid</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sale">Salé</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chellah">Chellah</a> and fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barghawata">Barghawata</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-ifran">Ifranid</a> territories in the second half of the 11th century, and the tribe was dispersed or absorbed into the new order. Ifranid groups survived in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, where some served as soldiers.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 742 CE – 1066 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:74.47%;width:6.45%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>742 CE – 1066 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tlemcen</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abu Qurra, Ya'la ibn Muhammad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sufri Kharijism, later Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Berber, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a>, <a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Banu Ifran, Kharijite state of Tlemcen</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=904&amp;focus=banu-ifran-emirate" aria-label="Banu Ifran emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4647 915 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Banu Ifran emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4967 1171L6134 1224M4967 1171L4881 1071M4967 1171L4799 1289"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6134 1224h0M4881 1071h0M4799 1289h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4967 1171h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4967 1171h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tlemcen. <a href="/atlas?year=904&amp;focus=banu-ifran-emirate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
